Sorry about the delay... This PR is heading the right direction, I just don't like the naming. `MountSensitiveWithSystemd(... false)` does not suggest it's actually about skipping systemd.

Can there be `Mounter.SetSystemdUnit(false)` and store the flag in mounter struct, without any changes in `Mount` or `MountSensitive`?

Or even use option pattern:

```go
func NewWithFlags(mounterPath string,  options ...MounterOption) Interface {
    mnt := &Mounter{
		mounterPath: mounterPath,
		withSystemd: detectSystemd(),
	}
    for _, opt := range options {
        opt(mnt)
    }
    return mnt
}

type MounterOption func(*mounter)

func WithoutSystemd(mnt *mounter) {
    mnt.withSystemd=false
}
```

(Be careful with naming, "mount option" has a distinct meaning.)

@jsafrane Thanks, yes, i will change the name.
Your options are good directions, but the `Mounter` is global from kubelet, that means all the plugin will share the options if add mnt.withSystemd=false. If a driver plugin developer doesn't know the context, he/she could be confused for the output. As for other developers know this context, every time call mount() need to set this option also looks complex.
So i think using value copy can cover this problem:
```
func WithoutSystemd(mounter Interface) Interface {
	m, ok := mounter.(*Mounter)
	if ok {
		return &Mounter{
			mounterPath: m.mounterPath,
			withSystemd: false,
		}
	}
	return mounter
}
```

I am sorry, you're right, I missed kubelet has one global `Interface`.

`mount.WithoutSystemd(b.mounter).Mount()` does look even worse than `mount.MountSensitiveWithoutSystemd()` (or even `MountSensitiveWithoutSystemService()`. No flags, no configs, just a new method with a clear name.
